                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Structure**\n\nI'm currently dissecting the grid's structure, noting the 21x13 dimensions and the distinction between '0' passages and '8' walls. My focus is on how odd/even coordinates might represent vertices or edges within this maze.\n\n**Identifying Color Patterns**\n\nI'm observing that the '3' and '7' values seem tied to the parity of the sum of row and column indices. Odd sums are yielding '7', while even sums are producing '3'. This suggests a bipartite coloring or flood-fill mechanism is at play.\n\n**Revising Coloring Logic**\n\nMy previous assumption about '3' and '7' being solely tied to coordinate sum parity is incorrect. I'm now investigating how connected components of '0' cells influence the coloring, with a particular focus on the starting points of the flood fill. The observed pattern seems more complex than a simple bipartite division.\n\n",
